    "created_at": "2021-10-13T06:54:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-13T06:54:09Z",
    "body": "What an awful omission on my side, to clarify:\r\nThe HTML-bits should be in HTML\r\nThe Sanitizer interface, is likely going to be adopted into [W3C WebAppSec](https://github.com/WICG/sanitizer-api/issues/114).\r\n\r\nI don't have a very strong preference here but I do feel a need to reconcile the points that were made in another thread, which has unfortunately derailed quite a bit (`https://github.com/w3c/webappsec/issues/596`). \r\n- we really *need* solid maintenance and co-development of new HTML features with the Sanitizer, so that neither is breaking the other.\r\n- @mikewest made a (imho reasonable) point, that we would like to have a somewhat small and readable spec that focuses solely on the Sanitizer use case.\r\n\r\nI hope the summary is correct and satisfactory for both sides. I'm happy to work with y'all, if not.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
