    "created_at": "2021-12-01T12:18:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-01T12:18:51Z",
    "body": "With a bit of a delay, we've discussed that we will follow your suggestion to move things into the HTML spec directly.\r\n\r\nFor starters, I considered creating with an [element category](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-element-categories) that explains whether an element should \"allowed by the Sanitizer by default\" e.g., by following these steps:\r\n\r\n- add a category that we may called \"allowed by the sanitizer by default\" (very explicit in its intention or \"safe for untrusted content\" (less explicit, but maybe more accessible) to the list of Categories\r\n- add a section (where?) that explains what \"safe\" means (largely borrowing from the [Security Considerations](https://wicg.github.io/sanitizer-api/#security-considerations) in the wicg spec).\r\n- add the category element definitions\r\n\r\n@domenic and I'd really like to hear your feedback here :)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
